# Your identities for the servers of this copy. Get ready (Servers) writes the real file, .harness/.env, after a test of the way in passed:
# you need not write it by hand. Never commit, share or paste .harness/.env; the agent cannot read it, and `harness reinstall` carries it.
#
# One line per value: HARNESS_SERVER_<ALIAS>_<FIELD>=value (the alias in capitals, - as _). A value with spaces or quotes is in double quotes.
#
# A server of the company pack (company/tools/servers.json) needs only your identity:
# HARNESS_SERVER_ORDERS_DEV_ACCOUNT=EXAMPLE\your-id
# HARNESS_SERVER_ORDERS_DEV_PASSWORD="your password"
#
# A server of your own also says what it is (its kind must be one of .harness/kinds/):
# HARNESS_SERVER_MY_DB_ALIAS=my-db
# HARNESS_SERVER_MY_DB_KIND=sqlserver
# HARNESS_SERVER_MY_DB_ENV=dev
# HARNESS_SERVER_MY_DB_AUTH=sql
# HARNESS_SERVER_MY_DB_HOST=localhost
# HARNESS_SERVER_MY_DB_PORT=1433
# HARNESS_SERVER_MY_DB_ACCOUNT=sa
# HARNESS_SERVER_MY_DB_PASSWORD="..."
